WEBVTT

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:06.360
"It will be fine, you can do it..."

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.960
"Onii-chan, you of all people can save this world."

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.030
"I will be okay."

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.580
"Onii-chan, I will always be together with you, so..."

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.870
"So... so..."

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:25.210
"Take care of Meguri, okay?"

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.190
It's done.

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:44.360
Come with me next Saturday like you promised.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.700
We'll meet at 10 in the morning.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.620
I won't forgive you if you are late or stand me up.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:53.080
I will be waiting,

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.230
Onii-chan.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:58.410
I mean, Morals-kun.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:33.760
Hey, Utaha-senpai...

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:35.620
What is it, Morals-kun?

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:38.720
I'd prefer it if you didn't talk to me when I'm reading.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.860
How long are you planning to stay here?

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:41.850
Well,

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:44.940
I guess until I'm done reading through this <i>Monogatari</i> series.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:50.250
<i>Certainly, at that moment, I wanted to consider her words nothing but a joke,</i>

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.660
<i>but based on what I know about her,</i>

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.750
<i>the woman called Kasumigaoka Utaha is,</i>

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.520
<i>at least as far as reading books is concerned,</i>

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:02.330
<i>much more foolish, arrogant, and pure than anybody could possibly imagine.</i>

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:07.090
Stay put at least until I've read this one volume.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.590
You'll just be a nuisance if you make too much noise at a bookstore.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:12.320
That's right, it's a bookstore.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:16.260
It's not a place to read books for free, but to buy them.

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:21.180
Can't be helped then.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.230
In that case, I'll go buy these books,

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:24.430
so wait for a moment.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.810
I'm not going to grumble that I would've liked you to do so to begin with.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.920
Come on, let's go, Morals-kun.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:34.820
W-Wait a little!

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:38.050
You said you'd carry my things,

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:40.290
but we've only been to one shop and you're already in trouble.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:41.500
You're just all talk, aren't you?

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:46.450
I couldn't imagine you picking up all the volumes of a series in the first shop.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:47.880
There's no helping it.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:52.540
I've been so occupied with writing for so long now that I haven't been able to read anything at all.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.340
Sorry to make you wait, Eriri!

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:58.260
So slow!

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.140
Where did you slack off, Megumi?!

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:06.270
I rather think I did quite well for a girl who was still in her pyjamas when she got called out half an hour ago.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.640
Those two left already because it took you so long to come!

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.000
Which two?

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.310
Listen and be shocked!

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.720
That Kasumigaoka Utaha and-

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:15.940
Ah, I got it,

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.780
you don't need to explain any further.

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:19.990
So, once more,

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:23.700
Utaha-senpai, good job finishing the scenario!

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.270
Thank you, Morals-kun,

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.630
but I'm at a good part right now, so be quiet.

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:30.400
Um...

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:35.760
You know, Utaha-senpai, this celebration is happening at your insistence.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.660
Can't be helped.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:40.670
Rather than appetite or lust, I'm currently driven by my thirst for knowledge.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:43.770
Stop nonchalantly concealing your questionable desires!

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.580
I'll be done reading soon,

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:49.650
so Morals-kun, eat whatever you want until then.

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:50.390
Yes...

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.190
Hey, Utaha-senpai.

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:09.440
What?

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:11.200
When you've finished that,

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.240
to satisfy your thirst for knowledge even more,

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.580
should we go to a movie?

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:15.940
Right...

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.290
That might be nice too.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:18.180
All right, it's decided!

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:20.430
What should we watch...

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:25.810
A disappointing live-action adaptation which torments those who love the original work might be nice.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.810
I wonder if there's anything like that.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:30.450
I'm reminded of several,

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:31.900
but I'm not going to tell you their titles!

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.230
They're not here...

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:37.110
Sheesh, where did those two go?!

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.340
Come to think of it, Eriri...

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.680
What is it?

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:44.440
How did you know they were together?

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.490
How did you happen to be where they were?

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:47.980
That's...

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.330
I happened to see them when I was shopping.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:51.750
Happened to, huh?

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:56.510
Come to think of it, we once met at
Rokutenba Mall by coincidence, too.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:06:00.220
I hate perceptive girls like you.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:00.930
Huh?

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:02.830
W-What, it's the truth!

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:05.170
No matter who says what, a coincidence is a coincidence-

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:09.020
Hey, isn't that Aki-kun and Kasumigaoka-senpai over there?

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:10.310
Where, where?

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:13.520
There, queuing for the movie theatre.

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:15.520
You're right!

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.050
Well done, Megumi!

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:21.140
That astuteness which picks up on only the good bits is just like you!

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:23.820
Um, can I go home now?

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:30.250
Well, it was inevitable since it is a sequel to the television series,

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:32.210
but it really was pointless.

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:33.510
You think?

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:35.210
The new character was cute,

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:37.610
and the final scene was touching.

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:40.300
That's thanks to character design and production values.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.930
Even though the script is clichéd at best,

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:48.180
just because the art, the music, or the voice actors' performances are good, people decide to like it anyway.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:49.840
But you know,

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.860
rather than saying that the script was bad,

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:57.190
I think honestly praising it for the good characters and music make you happier as a fan.

00:06:57.190 --> 00:07:02.010
Such blind believers end up corrupting the creators before you know it.

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:04.730
It's no use telling that to a leecher like me.

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:11.710
I don't want to hear such irresponsible things from the director who is going to make my scenario into a game.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:13.840
Listen, Morals-kun.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:18.880
Be sure you have the eyes and courage to be able to say what's good is good and what's bad is bad.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:20.970
I get the "eyes",

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:22.170
but courage?

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:23.190
Yes.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:27.470
The courage to mercilessly berate even my own work if you think it's bad,

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:28.260
is what I mean.

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.730
Won't you get angry if I do that?

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:32.880
Of course I won't!

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:37.010
There's nothing I appreciate more than the honest opinion of those who consume my works.

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:38.130
I-I see.

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:39.130
Well,

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:42.280
I will sulk a lot, though.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:45.530
I'm ready to not speak to you for a month.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:50.440
And if your opinion misses the mark, I'll never talk to you again.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:53.000
I don't want to take such a scary gamble!

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:57.180
Are you calming down?

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:58.620
Y-Yes...

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:02.040
Sorry for you having to see me in this state...

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.340
It's okay.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:06.600
You're quite sensitive, aren't you, Eriri.

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:08.010
But you know,

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:12.040
I can't believe Mariko was promoted to the main heroine even though she had such bad luck in the main story...

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.600
That happened?

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:19.400
I mean, Shouhei, the main character, decided to forget about Ui, the main heroine of the TV series, and move on!

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:20.450
That means,

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:24.990
the only one beside him is Mariko, who has been watching him ever since they were children!

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:26.090
I wonder if that's true.

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:27.530
It is!

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:28.740
I'm so happy!

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:32.750
I'm so happy it didn't end with the last episode of the TV series!

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.750
Well, enough about that.

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:37.620
Shouldn't we get going soon, too?

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:41.880
More importantly, I haven't talked about The Prism enough!

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.920
The childhood friend route truly is great.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:50.680
Well then,

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:53.100
good job today.

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:54.520
Good job!

00:08:57.270 --> 00:09:00.460
You really seem tired, too.

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:02.520
Just how much did you buy, Utaha-senpai?

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:04.800
You should have that delivered!

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:06.620
I want to read some of them right away,

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:08.530
so I'll take a lot home with me.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:15.040
Well, be that as it may,

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:18.190
good job finishing the scenario, too.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:22.000
Sorry for taking longer than expected.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.150
It's fine!

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:25.560
I know that you have to write your novels, too,

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.710
so I was the one who asked for the impossible.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:30.430
Anyway, with this, I'm done with my responsibilities.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:34.480
I may not be able to show up for the circle activities from now on.

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:36.430
I still have my own novels to write, you know.

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:40.940
I also have to start thinking about my future,

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:44.330
though I'm doing it quite a lot later than most.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:46.570
I see.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:53.710
Well, I think I'll get endorsements, so it's not such a big deal.

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:54.850
I-Is that so?

00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:58.040
Of course, with your grades...

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:00.860
Apparently there are currently two openings I can be referred to.

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:03.160
One is a university in the Kansai area...

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:04.460
K-Kansai?!

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:07.340
Utaha-senpai, won't you stay here?

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.920
...and the other one is fifteen minutes by train from here.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:10.920
Huh?

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:13.390
I'm currently at a loss as to which one I should pick.

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:16.470
Morals-kun, which one do you think is better?

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:17.890
M-Me?

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:22.050
The department I want to go to is ranked higher in the Kansai university,

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:26.260
but living alone apart from my parents would be a pain too.

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:31.110
Having said that, it's not like I'm uninterested in living freely, being able to do what I want.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:35.660
Hey, Morals-kun.

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:43.830
Why are you so flustered?

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.130
Don't tease me!

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:52.090
Yeah!

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:53.360
Hey...

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:55.230
Coming in!

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:56.850
How about this?

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:59.600
I think it'd suit you.

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:00.850
This too!

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:03.250
Actually, most things suit you.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:06.770
Your skin is pale, your hair glistening, and you're slender, after all!

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:09.450
It's worth finding matching clothes!

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:11.440
There's this blouse, too.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.520
Hey, wait a minute, Megumi!

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.030
Ah, are you going with the one you're trying on now?

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:17.840
That's not what I'm talking about!

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:20.300
What are we doing here?!

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:22.210
Picking casual wear for you, of course.

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:24.290
You can't just always wear a jersey-

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:27.670
While you're being so carefree, we lost those two, didn't we?!

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:29.890
Huh, that was because you wanted to talk about the movie-

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:32.870
There's no point in bringing up the past at this point!

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:35.610
Anyway, we'll have to go look for them again right now!

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:38.590
Wasn't that enough for today?

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:43.380
Even disregarding the fundamental question of whether or not it's okay to play a stalker to begin with.

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:44.640
What are you saying?!

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:48.080
There's no way of knowing what those two will end up guilty of if you let them be!

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:50.670
It may lead to a collapse of the circle!

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:56.710
Kasumigaoka-senpai messaged me earlier that she's not going to do anything today, so you can be at ease.

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:57.990
What?

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.490
Well then, I'm going this way.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.570
Utaha-senpai!

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:11.420
I think staying here would be better than Kansai.

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:17.180
If you are here, even when you're in university,

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:20.180
we may be able to make another game or something together.

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:25.940
Still, if you were to say that you never want to join forces with me again, I could do nothing but step back...

00:12:26.420 --> 00:12:30.350
If it comes to that, this year may be the last time we make a game...

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:34.190
That may be the result, but...

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:42.700
Even so, I don't want to be the one to rule out the possibility.

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:53.160
So that's your reaction.

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:55.920
You're such a bad boy, Morals-kun.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:04.930
In that case, I'm giving you a chance.

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:09.100
The scenario for the last route of our game.

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:14.180
But Utaha-senpai, you said that what you gave me earlier was the last...

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:15.880
I rewrote it afterwards.

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:19.340
The developments and the conclusion are different from that one.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:20.110
Wha-

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:25.970
That is another possibility for us... for our game.

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.450
S-Senpai-?

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.530
Morals-kun, I want you to decide.

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:32.750
The earlier first version, or that second version...

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:34.790
Which will you pick?

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:40.190
And what should I do in the future?

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:45.060
<i>You have to read it.</i>

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:47.250
<i>You have to decide.</i>

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:50.270
<i>After all, you are not just a fan now,</i>

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:52.920
<i>but the director.</i>

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:10.000
I wonder if Aki-kun is not home.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.970
We were supposed to meet at 10 in the morning, weren't we?

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:15.940
C-Could it be that he hasn't returned after last night?

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:19.130
Maybe he's drinking his morning coffee in a hotel room at this very moment?

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:20.740
You know, Eriri,

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:24.650
having a vivid imagination may be an asset for an artist,

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:30.140
but getting dragged into your delusions is somewhat troublesome, or rather, quite unbearable.

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:33.900
A-Anyway, I'll just drop into Tomoya's room.

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:36.180
But entering without permission...

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:38.900
I'll just confirm whether or not he is here!

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:43.660
If we end up skipping our circle activities today, the one most affected...

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:45.000
...will be him!

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:45.700
I see, that's true.

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:47.100
Not here.
I see, that's true.

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:47.920
I see, that's true.

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.180
Sheesh!

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.000
Huh?!

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:53.500
Excuse us!

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:56.740
M-Megumi, you...

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:58.000
Hm?

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:08.120
Um...

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:09.180
Morning!

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:11.590
You're here?

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:14.440
Are you going to cry or greet us? Pick one!

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:17.440
Oh!

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.320
What is this?

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:25.660
"In order to protect each other, the former big brother
and little sister, now lovers, decide to fight the enemy!"

00:15:26.140 --> 00:15:28.120
Until this point, it's the same as the current scenario.

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:31.760
But in this new scenario Utaha-senpai gave me yesterday,

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.710
the developments after this are completely different!

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:38.130
Ah, so the siblings being lovers thing was a no-go after all?

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:39.090
No!

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:42.270
2D will never lose to T**!

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:43.770
If anything, the opposite!

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:45.080
In this scenario,

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:47.020
rather than the present-time lover, Meguri,

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:50.550
the consciousness of the little sister from a previous life, Ruri, rises to the front!

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.610
You mean, a rare and unexpected heroine switch?

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:53.800
Exactly!

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:57.910
From this point onwards, the world of the forbidden brother-sister love goes deeper than ever!

00:15:57.910 --> 00:15:58.720
Go ahead, Katou!

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:02.030
Wait a moment, this line is...

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:03.100
Don't say that, Katou!

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:04.040
Break out of your shell!

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:05.280
Overcome your barriers!

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:09.200
Devote all of your strength to this story!

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:10.870
U-Um...

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:14.980
"I love you, Onii-chan. I won't ever give you to anyone else again."

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:17.190
There's the hyper-yandere little sister version "Onii-chan"!

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:19.250
You're way too excited.

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:22.810
But the two of them couldn't live happily like that for very long.

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:25.180
In order to save this collapsing world,

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:28.160
they needed the power concealed within Ruri to destroy the demon.

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:32.520
However, that power could only be activated by wearing away Ruri's memory!

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:36.880
In other words, it's the ultimate dilemma of whether you'll save the world or your little sister?

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:41.730
Um, but if you pick your sister and the world is destroyed, won't you end up losing everything anyway?

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:44.950
Katou, you aren't qualified to comment on the <i>sekaikei</i> genre!

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:45.910
Ah, yes,

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:48.660
I don't have the qualifications or even the knowledge, so whatever.

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:51.450
Then, finally, the final, decisive battle!

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:56.810
Even when facing the ultimate enemy, the main character Souma can't bear to erase Ruri, his beloved little sister!

00:16:56.810 --> 00:17:01.560
But Ruri, truly loving her so weakened big brother from the bottom of her heart,

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:03.140
makes the decision in his stead.

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:04.130
By erasing herself,

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:07.370
leaving behind the world, no, her sole big brother in this present life,

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:11.590
she makes her most proper and saddest possible choice!

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:13.210
Your turn, Katou!

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:14.120
Um...

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:15.640
This line?

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:18.820
"I'm in love with you, Onii-chan."

00:17:18.820 --> 00:17:22.150
"I was very happy to be able to meet you."

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:24.880
"This is the truth."

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:27.440
Ruri, wait, don't go!

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.070
I don't want this to be the end!

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:30.910
Oh, that was nothing.

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:35.640
Well? How's this scenario?

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:37.660
It's interesting.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.210
The first one is good too,

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:40.880
but this is also really good.

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:41.780
Right?!

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:43.540
Yeah, it's really moving.

00:17:44.030 --> 00:17:48.760
If I had read it alone in silence without all the commentary and screaming, I might have cried too.

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:50.300
Eriri, it made you cry too, didn't it?

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:52.020
This is clearly where the evangelist of tragic love,

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:53.540
the heart-breaking author,

00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:57.020
Kasumi Utako, that is, Kasumigaoka Utaha-senpai, has poured her soul into-

00:17:57.020 --> 00:18:00.020
Isn't this just making it all over again?!

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:03.020
At least take in the story and be impressed by the quality!

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:05.270
Yeah, maybe I was impressed!

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:10.530
If I wasn't responsible for the art nor had to come up with a bunch of new material at this point!

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:11.860
And anyway, Tomoya,

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:16.620
is it really fine to change to this scenario?

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:17.770
That's...

00:18:17.770 --> 00:18:21.370
It changes the interpretation of everything we have been making until now.

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:24.760
Even the theme of the scenario may flip on its head.

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:26.380
Yeah.

00:18:27.090 --> 00:18:32.140
For the art, I'd need to redo everything, starting with the facial expressions of the character illustrations.

00:18:32.950 --> 00:18:34.150
You're right.

00:18:34.150 --> 00:18:36.420
What's more, the main heroine changes.

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:37.390
I know.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:41.390
Meguri may still be on the packaging, like until now.

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:47.360
But the true heroine the story focuses on has become Ruri.

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:50.870
Meguri would be nothing but a window dressing heroine.

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:52.420
This sense of loss...

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:53.790
This pain...

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:55.810
But this exhilarating feeling...

00:18:55.810 --> 00:18:59.410
This truly is the same Kasumi Utako as in Metronome of Love.

00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:03.180
You've read Metronome of Love?

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:05.320
J-Just rumours on the net!

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:08.250
I haven't read even a line from that woman's novels!

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.170
Whoa, what a mean reader!

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:11.770
Or well, you aren't even her reader.

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:13.160
Anyway,

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:14.310
what are we going to do?

00:19:14.310 --> 00:19:15.920
Are we really switching to this?

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:17.230
So what this means is,

00:19:17.230 --> 00:19:23.470
today, our circle will discuss whether or not to include Utaha-senpai's new scenario in the game!

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:24.510
No way.

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:30.000
Don't leave such an important decision to the artist who's about to blow her deadlines!

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:36.200
But thinking together, deciding together and overcoming it together, that's who we, Blessing Software, are...

00:19:36.630 --> 00:19:37.830
No.

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:41.210
This decision determines the direction of the project.

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:44.200
So the producer and director have to decide.

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:46.720
Doesn't that mean just me alone?

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:49.960
If you were to consult someone,
shouldn't it be the one who wrote it?

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:52.610
Though she doesn't seem to have been invited today.

00:19:52.610 --> 00:19:55.080
Utaha-senpai is done with her part,

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:57.630
and apparently she's almost in trouble with her novel deadlines.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:00.780
But she could spare a day to flirt with a guy.

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:02.810
Don't spread misinformation like you'd seen it!

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:04.760
What, misinformation?

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:08.810
So what I saw yesterday all over the place was nothing but illusions?

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:11.150
Why were you all over the place?!

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:12.960
That's...

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:14.430
Um...

00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:15.560
That's right!

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:17.620
I was hanging out with Megumi, of course!

00:20:17.620 --> 00:20:20.480
Why did that sound like you just remembered it now?!

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:22.200
Hey, isn't that right, Megumi?

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:26.120
Please, answer "yeah, that's right", like you always do!

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:32.260
Ah, I'm playing a game right now, so could you two perhaps be a little quieter?

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:36.440
Katou, it's quite rare that you play a game by yourself.

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:37.730
What game is it?

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:39.590
It's just a demo version.

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:43.380
Apparently it's a doujin game which is supposed to be released at winter Comiket this year.

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:46.160
Huh, it's the same genre as ours?

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:48.650
So their space might be close to ours.

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:50.270
What is the circle called-

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:54.370
Ah, actually, they e-mailed me about it earlier.

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:56.860
Hey, wait a minute, this art...

00:20:57.470 --> 00:20:59.320
Izumi-chan?

00:20:59.930 --> 00:21:01.790
Rouge en rouge?

00:21:08.820 --> 00:21:10.080
Onii-chan.

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:13.340
What is it,

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:15.260
Izumi?

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:17.920
I'm cold.

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:20.890
Should we buy hot azuki soup on the way?
